> such:
> {.i lo ka ce'u srana ce'u cu ka ce'u ce'u ckini lo ka co'e}
> Things that are relevant to each other are simply related by an obvious 
> relationship.
>

That's what I was afraid of. And I don't like it. Then we don't have a 
gismu for "topic", do we?
If {srana} is about topic then ckini makes sense with all it's three places.
Then {srana} is not just a subset of {ckini}. It gives us topicalisation in 
the form of a predicate (which is very nice) but which is still poorly 
understood (remember recent discussions on {kau} acting as a topic marker 
etc.) 
 

